# Build artifacts for the Alpine foundation.
#
# Upstream NextUI's own .gitignore is not modified (this fork makes zero edits
# to NextUI files), so everything we generate is ignored here instead. A
# .gitignore applies to its own directory and everything below it, so this
# covers alpine/ without touching the repo root.

# abuild/abuild working dirs
aports/*/src
aports/*/pkg

# Build output tree. Anchored with a leading slash on purpose: a bare `out/`
# matches any directory named out at any depth, which silently swallowed the
# vendored bootloader blobs in bootloader/<board>/out/.
/out/

# fetched sources and toolchain checkouts
dl/

# kernel build tree
build-bootloader-tmp/

# built images
*.img
*.img.zst
*.erofs
*.tar.zst
*.apk

# local repo index
local-repo/

# the vendored board scripts are Minime's; keep our own additions executable
!boards/*.sh

# ── the vendored bootloader blobs are NOT build artifacts ───────────────────
# alpine/bootloader/<board>/out/ holds committed third-party binaries, not
# anything this repo generates -- see alpine/bootloader/README.md for provenance
# and licensing. We do not build u-boot, so these must be tracked or every image
# build warns about a missing bootloader and emits something unbootable.
#
# These negations must stay LAST: the *.img rule above would otherwise re-ignore
# idbloader.img, and git cannot re-include a file inside an ignored directory
# unless the directory itself is un-ignored first.
!bootloader/
!bootloader/**
